            <ArticleTitle>Recurrent sigmoid volvulus in a sixteen-year-old boy: case report and review of the literature.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1434-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors describe a 16-year-old boy in whom 3 episodes of sigmoid volvulus (SV) occurred over a period of 7 weeks, each time reduced by endoscopy. The child subsequently underwent a successful sigmoid resection with primary anastamosis. Several months after surgery, he remains free of symptoms and is doing well. A review of the literature illustrates the approach to this problem from ancient times until now.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
